    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d857">

                <pb facs="1058" n="1050" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg1050"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.5314/7</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 439</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-01-13">January 13, 1939</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Reference is made to your despatch No. 686
                    of July 2, 1938, which reported the receipt of a Foreign Office note No. W
                    7459/156/36 of July 1, 1938, in reply to the Embassy’s representations with
                    regard to the right of the United States to be consulted in connection with
                    certain modifications of the frontier between Tanganyika Territory and
                    Mozambique.</p>
                <p>Having consulted with the American consular representatives at Nairobi and
                    Lourenço Marques, neither of whom perceive objection to the frontier changes in
                    question, the Department authorizes you to <pb facs="1059" n="1051"
                        xml:id="pg1051"/> inform the Foreign Office that the Government of the
                    United States assents to the alterations in the frontiers between Tanganyika
                    Territory and Mozambique as set forth in the notes exchanged at Lisbon on May
                    11, 1936 and December 28, 1937 between Great Britain and Portugal.<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d857-f1"/></p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner
                            Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d857-f1" n="10" xml:id="d857-f1-content">
                <p>In accordance with this instruction the assent of the United States was given in
                    a note to the British Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs, dated January 24,
                    1939, not printed (741.5314/10).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
